        "caption": "Verdance, where the sky went dark first."
      },
      "columns": [
        "<p>MAXIMA STATION - The Maximus Core, the forge-star that has lit the galaxy for ten thousand years, cracked at 0400 station time. Its light, held in ten star-shards, was flung across the Hundred Worlds.</p><p>Within the hour the lanes to Emberreach went quiet. By nightfall The Shallows had stopped answering.</p>",
        "<p>\"We have never lost a lane before,\" said a dock chief at the station, who asked not to be named. \"Now we are losing them one after another.\"</p><p>The Courier Corps has grounded all but one pilot. Station sources confirm the courier known as Max has been given the job of bringing the shards home.</p>",
        "<p>Traders at Waystation Ceres report pirate skiffs moving into the empty lanes. Couriers are advised to fly armed.</p><p>Crystal gates have reportedly sealed every sector beyond The Cradle. Scholars believe each gate answers only to its own pair of shards.</p>"
      ],
      "briefs": [
        ["GLOOP SEASON EARLY", "Verdance farmers report hopping slimes in record numbers. Harmless alone; never alone."],
        ["LIGHTHOUSE STILL TURNS", "The old station in The Shallows keeps its light burning, though nobody has heard from its crew."],
        ["TRADING POSTS OPEN", "Extra lives 100 credits, repairs 20, med kits 50. One of each per visit."]
